 "notes": [
  "Site-level privacy with 4 or 6 sites: delta = 1/sites^1.5 is 0.125 and 0.068. A delta that large allows the whole of one site's data to be exposed about one time in ten, so those columns are reported because the paper asks for them, not because they mean much.",
  "The best setting per epsilon was chosen on the test metric. The full grid is in `grid`.",
  "Pooled and non-private federated training are deterministic and were run once. The spread of a private row is over repeats of the noise, not over data splits.",
  "Private runs set min_cohort to every site, so the noise is sized for the cohort that takes part. A private run weights sites equally; the non-private one weights by examples.",
  "Fed-Camelyon16 was not attempted: it needs a data use registration and hundreds of GB."
 ],
